   "subject": "Can I vary gradient colors based on another variable in a heatmap?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p>Hi,<br><br>I am making a heatmap and using 3 variables.  They respectively represent: the X-axis, Y-axis and the intensity of the color.  I want to use a 4th to change the color.  Can this be done?  <br><br>Here&#39;s a mock-up of what I have:<br><br><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-96Am0oPB3zM/ViZfQDanQNI/AAAAAAAAABA/QUrfCuMqtEs/s1600/mock.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-96Am0oPB3zM/ViZfQDanQNI/AAAAAAAAABA/QUrfCuMqtEs/s1600/mock.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368561385000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1sDxx4nreY77K1V2CrnSiE\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-96Am0oPB3zM/ViZfQDanQNI/AAAAAAAAABA/QUrfCuMqtEs/s320/mock.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"320\" width=\"320\"></a></p>Days are on the X-axis.  I&#39;d really love to be able to turn the weekend days blue and keep the weekdays green.  <br><br>Here&#39;s the code:<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"> m_date </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2015-09-13&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2015-09-14&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2015-09-15&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br> M_date </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> M_hour </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">13</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">13</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">13</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> M_Count </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> M_WE </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Mock</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">M_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> M_hour</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> M_Count</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> M_WE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> p1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> qplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">M_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> M_hour</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fill</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">M_Count</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Mock</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;tile&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> p1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> p1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> scale_x_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> scale_y_reverse</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> scale_fill_gradient</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">low </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;white&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> high </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;green2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">print</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br><table><tbody><tr><td>I want to set the color using: M_WE.   I was able to create new columns for weekend and weekday counts, and two separate graphs but then was not able to combine them.<br><br>Thanks in Advance,<br>Dustin<br><br></td>\r\n            \r\n<td><br></td></tr></tbody></table><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
