   "id": "B3EBsqQkCgAJ",
   "from": "Brandon Hurr",
   "author": "27405c4b711a1080",
   "date": "2015-10-20T18:00:32Z",
   "subject": "Re: Can I vary gradient colors based on another variable in a heatmap?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Something like this: <div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\" size=\"1\">ggplot(Mock, aes(M_date, M_hour, fill=M_Count, alpha= M_WE)) +</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\" size=\"1\">geom_tile() +</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\" size=\"1\">scale_x_date() +</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\" size=\"1\">scale_y_reverse() +</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\" size=\"1\">scale_fill_gradient(low = &quot;yellow&quot;, high= &quot;darkblue&quot;)</font></div></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\" size=\"1\"><br></font></div>Thanks for the MRE. <div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\" size=\"1\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\" size=\"1\"><br></font></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Oct 20, 2015 at 10:57 AM, Brandon Hurr <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">brando...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Sounds like you want to use two color scales. That&#39;s not possible. <div><br></div><div>Is there a way you can create a new variable between the two you want your color based upon to determine color? You could set one as an alpha scale and use M_WE as a color? That way intensity of color could be linked to one scale and the other variable is the color? </div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Oct 20, 2015 at 8:47 AM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dusti...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p>Hi,<br><br>I am making a heatmap and using 3 variables.  They respectively represent: the X-axis, Y-axis and the intensity of the color.  I want to use a 4th to change the color.  Can this be done?  <br><br>Here&#39;s a mock-up of what I have:<br><br><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-96Am0oPB3zM/ViZfQDanQNI/AAAAAAAAABA/QUrfCuMqtEs/s1600/mock.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-96Am0oPB3zM/ViZfQDanQNI/AAAAAAAAABA/QUrfCuMqtEs/s1600/mock.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368561395000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2MSm1eCU7iGlo13v8DQK8e\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-96Am0oPB3zM/ViZfQDanQNI/AAAAAAAAABA/QUrfCuMqtEs/s320/mock.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"320\" width=\"320\"></a></p>Days are on the X-axis.  I&#39;d really love to be able to turn the weekend days blue and keep the weekdays green.  <br><br>Here&#39;s the code:<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"> m_date </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2015-09-13&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2015-09-14&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2015-09-15&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br> M_date </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">m_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> M_hour </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">13</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">13</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">12</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">13</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> M_Count </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> M_WE </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Mock</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">M_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> M_hour</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> M_Count</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> M_WE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> p1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> qplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">M_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> M_hour</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fill</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">M_Count</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Mock</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;tile&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> p1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> p1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> scale_x_date</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> scale_y_reverse</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> scale_fill_gradient</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">low </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;white&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> high </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;green2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">print</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br><table><tbody><tr><td>I want to set the color using: M_WE.   I was able to create new columns for weekend and weekday counts, and two separate graphs but then was not able to combine them.<br><br>Thanks in Advance,<br>Dustin<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br><br></font></span></td>\r\n            \r\n<td><br></td></tr></tbody></table><span><font color=\"#888888\"><br></font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368561395000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0TlPJfxu2J2CaeNWlwO2eu\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nTo post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nTo unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\nMore options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368561395000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3izDbI-Y5_Miduq0ondClo\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><br>\r\n<br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;ggplot2&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368561395000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3RyVM5iS4uoMWprnLhpKP-\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n</div></div></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n"
