     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>On Tuesday, October 20, 2015 at 1:41:36 PM UTC-4, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">dusti...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><br></p>Hi,<br><br>I am making a heatmap and using 3 variables.  They respectively represent: the X-axis, Y-axis and the intensity of the color.  I want to use a 4th to change the color.  Can this be done?  <br><br>Here&#39;s a mock-up of what I have:<br><br><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><a style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-96Am0oPB3zM/ViZfQDanQNI/AAAAAAAAABA/QUrfCuMqtEs/s1600/mock.jpg\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-96Am0oPB3zM/ViZfQDanQNI/AAAAAAAAABA/QUrfCuMqtEs/s1600/mock.jpg&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792368561400000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2og0ycy-I4b0H0SjgCkHCu\"><img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-96Am0oPB3zM/ViZfQDanQNI/AAAAAAAAABA/QUrfCuMqtEs/s320/mock.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"320\" width=\"320\"></a></p>Days are on the X-axis.  I&#39;d really love to be able to turn the weekend days blue and keep the weekdays green.  <br><br>Here&#39;s the code:<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"> m_date </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;2015-09-13&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span>